# -*- mode:org;coding:utf-8 -*-
#+TITLE: vl-doc-*/VLX-namespace family: BricsCAD V26 provides it, contradicting the multidocument analysis
#+AUTHOR: Pascal J. Bourguignon
#+DATE: 2026-08-09

The multidocument analysis document
(clautolisp-multidocument-analysis.org) classifies ~vl-doc-export~ /
~vl-doc-import~ / ~vl-arx-import~ as existing "under --autocad only"
and says that under ~--bricscad~ they "should signal an
unsupported-feature condition rather than silently degrade".

Reality check on a real BricsCAD V26 (macOS, LispEx 26.0), via the
alpm verification probes (probe V-9, alpm CI job
verify:bricscad:macos, pipeline 2744343498, job 15791433487,
2026-08-09): the WHOLE family is present as SUBRs --
vl-doc-export, vl-doc-import, vl-doc-ref, vl-doc-set, vl-arx-import,
vl-list-exported-functions, vl-list-loaded-vlx, vl-vlx-loaded-p,
vl-unload-vlx, vl-acad-defun, vl-acad-undefun, vl-bb-ref, vl-bb-set.
~(vl-doc-export 'fn)~ executed in the document namespace returns T
(inert success; probe V-7).

This matches the Bricsys V25/V26 DevRef "VLX NameSpace Support"
page: since BricsCAD V18.2 (DEScoder v2.7+), the VLX-NameSpace
feature is supported for DES-encrypted LISP files, and these
functions are listed as supported.

* Suggested fix

- Correct the multidocument analysis (vl-doc-* is NOT AutoCAD-only;
  BricsCAD supports it for DES-encrypted namespace modules).
- The bricscad-* dialects should provide the family (inert T outside
  a namespace module, like the real engine), not signal
  unsupported-feature.
